            "target_entity_instance": "GEOS-Chem Classic",
            "target_entity_type": "Source",
            "paragraph": "In this study, we used GEOS-Chem version 13.2.1 in its high-performance implementation (GCHP). The flexibility and scalability of high resolution simulations in the standard offline version of GEOS-Chem (\u201cGEOS-Chem Classic\") are limited, as it relies on shared-memory parallelization and a rectilinear longitude-latitude grid (Martin et al., 2022). GCHP version 11, developed by Eastham et al. (2018), shares the same source code for physical and chemical mechanisms with GEOS-Chem Classic.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
