            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_SOURCE_COMPONENT",
            "target_entity_instance": "GFEDv4s",
            "target_entity_type": "SourceComponent",
            "paragraph": "In this study, we employed the Global Fire Emission Dataset version 4 (GFEDv4s), the built-in fire emission inventory in GCHP. GFEDv4s utilizes the Moderate Resolution Imaging Spectroradiometer (MODIS) Collection 5.1 MCD64A1 burned area product at 500-m spatial resolution to estimate the burned areas.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "MODIS",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MOUNTED_ON",
            "target_entity_instance": "Terra",
            "target_entity_type": "Platform",
            "paragraph": "GFEDv4s utilizes the Moderate Resolution Imaging Spectroradiometer (MODIS) Collection 5.1 MCD64A1 burned area product at 500-m spatial resolution to estimate the burned areas. It also incorporates 1-km thermal anomalies data from MODIS Terra and Aqua and 500-meter surface reflectance observations to account for the burned area of small fires in 0.25 degrees (BAsf) (van der Werf et al., 2017).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
